# Copy to .env and fill in real values. .env is git-ignored -- never commit credentials.
# See docs/LIVE_RAINFALL_AUDIT.md for how/whether to obtain these.

# IMD API Management Platform (https://api.imd.gov.in) API key.
# Obtaining one is NOT self-service: requires organisational registration on the portal AND, per IMD's own
# documentation, contacting the Nodal Officer (Dr. Sankar Nath, IMD New Delhi, sankar.nath@imd.gov.in) to be
# granted access under IMD's terms and conditions -- expect a manual approval process, not instant issuance.
# Leave unset/blank to run without live IMD data: IMDObservationProvider then reports itself as
# unavailable (reason: "not configured") rather than silently substituting fake data.
IMD_API_KEY=

# IMD API Management Platform JWT, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. This is a SEPARATE credential
# from IMD_API_KEY, not the same value: api.imd.gov.in requires BOTH headers, and returns three distinct 401
# bodies identifying which one is at fault ("API key missing" -> IMD_API_KEY; "Authorization header missing
# or invalid" -> this token; "Invalid or expired JWT token" -> key accepted, token stale). Verified
# empirically against the live endpoint -- see docs/LIVE_RAINFALL_AUDIT.md section 8c.
IMD_API_TOKEN=

# IMD station id for the current-weather endpoint (current_wx). Default 43003 = Mumbai-Santacruz, verified
# against IMD's own city.imd.gov.in linking convention (city.imd.gov.in/citywx/...?id=43003) -- see the audit
# doc. Override only if you have verified a different, more appropriate station id.
IMD_STATION_ID=43003

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEAVE THIS UNSET. Doppler Weather Radar integration boundary (IMDRadarNowcastProvider), disabled by design.
# Setting it does NOT enable radar: IMD publishes no documented radar data endpoint (the API reference's
# "Radar Image" entry is a dead anchor -- the document body ends at section 20), and the public radar imagery
# is a rendered picture whose top intensity bin is open-ended at >100 mm/h, below this project's own
# cloudburst (120 mm/h) and July 2005 (190.3 mm/h) scenarios, so it cannot represent the storms FloodNet
# models. The provider therefore always raises ProviderUnavailable and never estimates, decodes or
# substitutes a rainfall value from any other source.
# Enabling would require, at minimum: (a) a documented quantitative radar endpoint from IMD, (b) credentials
# authorised for it, (c) a resolved licence (mausam.imd.gov.in asserts copyright with no grant), (d) a product
# that resolves intensities above 100 mm/h, and (e) generalising RainfallScenario to accept a gridded field --
# it is currently a scalar [T] series, so no provider can supply spatial rainfall today (decision D-15).
# Evidence: docs/LIVE_RAINFALL_AUDIT.md sections 8b/8c; decisions D-14 and D-15 in docs/DECISIONS.md.
IMD_RADAR_ENABLED=


